The VA-OPD objective, method adapter, data preparation, evaluation aggregation,
configuration entrypoint, public recipes and tests in this release were rewritten
for Visual-Advantage On-Policy Distillation for Vision-Language Models.

The bundled training framework is derived from EasyR1, licensed under Apache-2.0,
which is itself based on veRL, Copyright 2024 Bytedance Ltd. and/or its affiliates.
Their copyright and license headers are retained in the corresponding source files.

The framework also includes Apache-2.0 adaptations by the
Awesome-Perception-Aware-RLVR authors, Copyright 2026, including multimodal
counterfactual-view builders, teacher worker plumbing and perception utilities.
These retained components keep their original copyright and license headers.
The rewritten verl/trainer/distillation.py does not retain the previous TRL-derived
loss implementation; other source-file attribution remains in place where applicable.

This release modifies the training driver and actor to reuse original-image teacher
logits for VA and KL, gather prompt statistics across data-parallel ranks, and enforce
paper settings and held-out validation. It also changes overlong-prompt handling to
raise an error, and keeps full resumable checkpoints.

Datasets and pretrained model weights are distributed by their respective owners
under their own licenses. Paper figures were supplied by the VA-OPD authors;
rights in the figures remain with their authors.
